---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import FlagBadge from '../../components/FlagBadge.astro';
import { absolute, href } from '../../lib/paths';

const title = 'Cappadocia balloon flags explained: green, yellow and red';
const description =
  'What the green, yellow and red flags on the official Cappadocia balloon status page mean, who decides, and how sectors and secondary regions work.';
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  structuredData={[
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Today', item: absolute('/', Astro.site) },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Flags explained', item: absolute('/flags/', Astro.site) },
      ],
    },
  ]}
>
  <h1>Balloon flags explained</h1>
  <p>
    Hot air balloon flights in Cappadocia need permission every day. The decision is published on the public page of the
    Kapadokya Slot Service Center as a coloured flag for each part of the flight area.
  </p>

  <h2>What each flag means</h2>
  <dl class="flags">
    <dt><FlagBadge flag="green" /></dt>
    <dd>
      Weather conditions are suitable and take-off is allowed. The official page says the final decision for the flight
      then rests with the pilot and the operating company, so a flight can still be cancelled on a green day.
    </dd>
    <dt><FlagBadge flag="yellow" /></dt>
    <dd>No take-off. The official page lists yellow together with red: approval for take-off is not possible.</dd>
    <dt><FlagBadge flag="red" /></dt>
    <dd>No take-off in that sector. Meteorological conditions have been judged unsuitable for the period shown.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Sectors A, B and C</h2>
  <p>
    The main flight area is split into three sectors, A, B and C, each with its own flag. Flags can differ between
    sectors on the same morning, so one company may fly while another stays on the ground.
  </p>

  <h2>Secondary flight regions</h2>
  <p>
    Regions 2 to 5 are secondary flight regions. Flights there need take-off confirmation from the Slot Service Center,
    granted by the controlling pilot or civil aviation staff, and companies can only request it for regions shown in green.
  </p>

  <h2>Times are published in UTC</h2>
  <p>
    Each flag comes with the time it was updated and the window it applies to, written in UTC. Türkiye is UTC+3 all
    year, so a window shown as 03:30–07:30 on the official page runs from 06:30 to 10:30 local time. This site converts
    every time to Türkiye time for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Who decides</h2>
  <p>
    Flights are permitted after a daily assessment of the weather by the Nevşehir coordination office of Türkiye's
    civil aviation authority (DGCA, SHGM in Turkish). This site only reads and records the published flags; it is not an
    official source.
  </p>

  <p><a href={href('/')}>See today's status</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .flags dt {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .flags dd {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
